          <caption>
            <p>Calcium Pyrophosphate Deposition Disease, Classification Criteria. This table outlines the&#x000a0;classification criteria for calcium pyrophosphate deposition (CPPD) disease, which requires a history of joint pain, swelling, or tenderness, along with imaging or crystal evidence of CPPD to confirm diagnosis.Abbreviations: CPP: calcium pyrophosphate; CPPD: calcium pyrophosphate deposition. Adapted from: Abhishek A, Tedeschi SK, Pascart T, et al. The 2023 ACR/EULAR classification criteria for calcium pyrophosphate deposition disease. <italic toggle="yes">Ann Rheum Dis.</italic> 2023;82(10):1248-1257. doi: 10.1136/ard-2023-224575.</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="Screenshot__2025-09-09__at__3.36.15xPM" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
        </fig>
      </floats-group>
      <floats-group id="article-27935.s18">
        <fig id="article-27935.image.f2" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
            <p>CPPD Cumulative Point-Based Criteria.&#x000a0;Items may be scored if they have been present at any point during the patient&#x02019;s lifetime. If multiple items in one domain apply, use the one with the highest score. Imaging of at least one symptomatic joint using CR, US, CT, or DECT is required. Adapted from: Abhishek A, Tedeschi SK, Pascart T, et al. The 2023 ACR/EULAR classification criteria for calcium pyrophosphate deposition disease. <italic toggle="yes">Ann Rheum Dis.</italic> 2023;82(10):1248-1257. doi: 10.1136/ard-2023-224575.</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="Screenshot__2025-11-30__at__2.40.51xPM" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
